# M1 walkthrough: model providers, model discovery, connectivity checks, model roles.
# Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension or the JetBrains HTTP client.
# Paste your SUPERAGENT_ADMIN_TOKEN and your provider's details below. Don't commit them.

@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:4111
@token = paste-your-admin-token-here
@providerUrl = https://your-provider.example/v1
@providerKey = paste-your-provider-key-here
@chatModel = your-chat-model

### Add an OpenAI-compatible provider. The key is stored encrypted and never returned.
# @name provider
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/providers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slug": "home", "name": "Home server", "baseUrl": "{{providerUrl}}", "apiKey": "{{providerKey}}" }

### List providers
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/providers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Discover its models (GET {providerUrl}/models)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/providers/{{provider.response.body.id}}/refresh-models
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Add a model by hand (servers without /models, or to mark an embedding model)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/providers/{{provider.response.body.id}}/models
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "modelId": "{{chatModel}}", "kind": "chat" }

### Run connectivity checks: chat, streaming with usage, tool calling (and embeddings if you pass embeddingModel)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/providers/{{provider.response.body.id}}/test
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "model": "{{chatModel}}" }

### Point the default model role at it
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/v1/settings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "models": { "default": { "provider": "home", "model": "{{chatModel}}" } } }

### Settings now
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/settings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Chat with the scratch agent through Mastra's routes (uses the default role)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/agents/scratch/generate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "messages": [{ "role": "user", "content": "In one sentence, what can you do?" }] }

### Rotate the key: applies to the next call, no restart
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/v1/providers/{{provider.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "apiKey": "{{providerKey}}" }
